In the past, we've nfs shared a single filesystem containing mail
messages across mutliple Ultrix workstations.  This makes it nice since
you can get your mail anywhere, and people don't have to know what
node you work on to send you mail.  And it's a lot easier than having
to worry about a central mail hub.

The problem is that we're adding OSF/1 workstations, and they aren't
being very cooperative.  It's no problem to mount the mail filesystem
and read messages from it, but it you try to mail anything to it you
get various kinds of locking problems.  I can find very little doc on
file locking with mail under Ultrix.  I'm beginning to suspect that
this was tightened up on OSF to get rid of some mail related security
problems. The question is whether this basic strategy will work at all
across Ultrix/OSF platforms and would it make any difference if I
moved the mail filesystem from Ultrix to OSF?

Thanks, and have a happy new year.

