In article <3dluhi$138s@ctsc.hkbc.hk>, s11976@ctsc.hkbc.hk (PM Wong) writes:
> We would not like to throw away the DECSERVERS 200. If the new Alpha running
> OSF/1 can do this load host function, it will be okay for us. So is there
> a version of DECSERVER 200 software for OSF/1 available yet (I seem to see it
> for VMS and Ultrix only) ? If yes, which version of OSF/1 is it for ?

  There's three pieces to this puzzle:

1) Availability of the load image (the software that gets loaded into the 
   DS200)

2) Availability of the loader code on the host (the ability to download
   servers via MOP)

3) Availability of LAT code on the host (the ability to accept LAT connec-
   tions)

  If you have all three, then things should work. The first item is easy -
load code for a given server is independent of the host OS. So, a PRO801ENG.
SYS (the DECserver 200 load code) file from any OS should work on any other
OS (though you may have to rename it to lower case, remove the .SYS part,
etc.).

  The second item should come with the operating system for multi-user sys-
tems from DEC (for PC's it comes with the load image kit). I would assume
that DEC's OSF/1 includes MOP, but I can't say for sure. Likewise for the
third item.

