: What are the formating and partitioning commands on this platform ?

: Go Steelers!

: Eric Davis 
: davis16@llnl.gov 

All you need to do is:

1) Hook up the drive and verify that it is visible from the >> prompt
   via a 'show device' command.

2) Boot the system and execute 'disklabel -wr' to label and/or partition
   the drive.

3) Then run execute the newfs command with the generic scsi device.  This
   will cause newfs to ask the drive what its characteristics are. (e.g. 
   'newfs /dev/rrz3c rzxx')

4) Mount the drive.

If you have any questions, feel free to ask.

