I had an extended discussion with Digital support about just these
issues for a news disk.

It's a messy picture.

First, ADVFS caches frags; I couldn't get a straight answer to which
utilities show that as free space (which it is) and which utilities
show it as used space (which it isn't).

Second, "overhead" gets fuzzy. Allegedly, if the file is small enough,
if data will be stored in the metadata area (i.e., inodes) and will
show up as "overhead", not data.

If you want to see some of this, do the following:

	# cd /news/.tags
	# ls -ls 1 M1 M-6 M-7 M-8 M-9

That's the metadata. Don't have a clue how to interpret any of this.

And, if you have the Advfs utilities:

	# shfragbf /news/.tags/1

When Digital Support offered this command and then couldn't explain the
output, I gave up and just threw another gig at my news spool. It was
easier.

Oh, and there's advfsstats, a utility for which there is no man page.
It gives great data and could likely answer many many questions about
what advfs is really up to. I'd love to see an explanation of the output.

	- Saul

