Ok, I posted in another thread about the problems in installing
DEC ADA.  Here is my solution.

All my previous problem happened when I logged in my machine
through LAT, and then "su".   Just awhile ago, I logged in
through a normal ttyp? login, and did "su".  Then I did 
"setld -v ADABASE320",  it completed successfully.  I then
went to one of my subdir and created "adalib" with no any
problem.

Conclusion: ADA installation verification will fail if done
   from an LAT login.  "amklib" will not create anything if
   the user logs in from an LAT tty.

Weird, isn't it?  This appears a bug, not feature :)

