Dear Pete,

If you feel that feature you referenced is major security problem in your 
environment, then you have always an option to setup special console
password to all the systems. Console password which has been forgotten can
be changed (or removed) only by field service engineer visiting your site
and replacing component on the system mother board.

Reason why console password is not active by default is the fact that most 
customer do not accept such functionality as default way to work.

If you feel that this level of security is not enough, you should consider 
upgrading to DEC OSF/1 AXP MLS+ version, which provides you:
