have found that there are a huge number of ethernet collisions under OSF/1
V3.0

Simply running the "netperf" benchmark, sending a tcp stream from one
Avanti to another, we get about 50% collision rate. (& about 6.7 Mbits/sec)
So for each 500 packets sent, there are 250 collisions according to monitor.

I've noticed that the "dos" documentation that comes with the "tu" (aka
TULIP card) says that the software can enable full duplex mode for the
10BaseT interface and wonder if that's causing the collisions.
We don't have a full duplex 10BaseT hub.

Going back to our AXP150 machines running OSF/1 V2.1 we get about 10%
collision rate when running netperf between two of the 150's (& about 
8.4 Mbits/sec data rate... better than the 233 machines!).

It looks like something is amiss in either the OSF tuning, or in the way
that the drivers are dealing with the hardware.

Anyone have any tips?  Seen this before?
