In DEC OSF/1, daemons are started by creating a script
in /sbin/init.d and creating a symbolic link to /sbin/rc3.d.
You can create links to directories other than /sbin/rc3.d
depending on your daemon's requirements for starting and
stopping at particular run levels, but rc3.d is the best
starting point.  You can see lots of examples in those
directories.  There are also man pages covering the whole
startup/shutdown system:

	man 8 { init | rc0 | rc2 | rc3 | shutdown }

Regards,
Todd Aven
