>I am trying to get my OSF/1 box to read an Ms-Dos partitioned and formatted
>hard disk. I have pulled over a freely available kit called MTOOLS which is
>supposed to allow you to do this.

>At the moment I can get MTOOLS to work with my systems floppy drive, but I 
>cannot get it to work with a hard disk.

>Has anyone managed to do this using MTOOLS or, any other piece of software.

MTOOLS works by accessing the raw device sequentially whilst respecting
or creating the MSDOS file system structures.  This is simple for
disks:  They have only one file system on.  A harddisk usually has
more.  Even if you happen to have only one partition there is
still the standard header ("Master Boot Record - MBR").
Thus, accessing hards disks is more tricky.

Do you have MTOOLS, V2.0? It says in the release.not file:

>New in the v2.0 release....
>
>        1) Support for multiple devices.  Mtools now supports:
>		multiple floppy disks (A:, B:, etc)
>		DOS partitions on a hard disk
>		DOS "images" such as those VP/ix uses.
>

You could probably access the raw disk and extract the data you want
by hand but this is somewhat brute force.

You could also try to put the beast in a PC and access the disk
via network.

