I wouldn't say "BSD-based".  You still need -lbsd, which looks very
similar to the -lBSD of HPUX :-)  And I couldn't find /etc/rc or 
/etc/rc.local when I had to add some daemons to the startup procedure.
I had to play with files in /sbin/rc3.d instead.  And last time I tried
