|>Has anybody a (preferably freely available) MPEG player that is
|>optimized for the Alpha architecture?

Yes, there are two MPEG-1 players which are optimized for Alpha included
with Multimedia Services for OSF/1.  The license for this is bundled with
the Alpha workstations and the software itself is both Factory Installed
and available on the Layered Products CD.

V1.3 includes an MPEG-1 Video player which is substantially faster than
the available public domain players and V1.4 which will be available on the
December Layered Products CD introduces support for MPEG-1 Audio decoding
as well as MPEG-1 Video, entirely in software, so you can now play back
MPEG Systems streams.

Make sure you have the MMERT130 or MMERT140 subset installed and look for
/usr/bin/mme/mpegplay (MPEG Video) or /usr/bin/mme/alphavcr (MPEG Systems).

