With the notable and for me a cause for some re-work, OSF/1's protocol stacks
are BSD style, linked into the kernel, as apposed to SYSV and Spec1170 infered
of being streams based.  I.E. socket() does NOT return a stream based fd.
Nor is OSF's X.25 stack streams based.  Not being streams based is an
issue for the OSI plug and play (yuk, yuk) streams based interfaces.

For me, it ment that the you can't poll() a socket, only select().
In my view, spec1170 didn't require protocol stacks to be streams based,
but, any company that thinks that not the way to go is sorely wrong.

