I have just commenced reading this newsgroup, so if this thread is of the FAQ
variety, please excuse me.

Could someone checkout my thought process (from their experience) in regard
to purchasing a startup DEC AlphaStation 200 4/166 system for running OSF/1?

The cheapest Alpha 200 4/166 packaged system is that which operates under
Windows NT.  Aside from the software, the differences between that packaged
system and the corresponding OSF/1 package are:
                      NT             OSF/1
	memory      16 Mbytes      32 Mbytes
	disk        340 Mbytes     1.05 Gbytes
	graphics    DEC864         ZLXp-E1
	
The other difference is the price.  That differential remains favourable to
the NT system even after pricing in the OSF/1 license and media on CD-ROM.
The question is, will OSF/1 work using 16 Mbytes of memory and the DEC864
graphics card.  Under OSF/1 my proposed system would be stand-alone running
Motif.  OSF/1 disk storage would be via an external 1 Gbyte disk connected
via the SCSI card.

The possibility of a dual boot of either NT or OSF/1 has appeal from a
research perspective.  So, is there any requirement to change the PAL code,
or what ever, to enable the Alpha chip to run under OSF/1 in stead of NT?

My argument that 16 Mbytes of memory will support OSF/1 is based on the
following.  The DECStation 5000, which was built on a MIPS R3000 RISC chip,
ran Ultrix using 8 Mbytes.  Now the kernal and filesystem of Ultrix is
thought to be comparable in complexity to that of OSF/1 and hence formed by
roughly the same number of executable instructions.  The R3000 and Alpha
chips are both RISC and have roughly comparable executable instructions.
The R3000 is 32 bit in comparison to the 64 bit of Alpha.  This factor of 2
thus increases the 8 Mbyte requirement of the DECStation to 16 Mbyte for the
AlphaStation.

The availability of a driver under OSF/1 for the DEC864 graphics card is a
complete unknown.  I cannot believe that DEC would supply support under
OSF/1 for a card that they designate for NT systems.  If that suspicion is
true, where can such a driver be obtained?

Any assistance in resolving these matters would be gratefully received.

