Nowhere in the foregoing discussion is there any mention of /etc/svc.conf,
which in all probability is the answer to your needs. Have a look at this
file, or run bindsetup to make your machine a client (does the same thing).
Note, if you were to go and install Resolv+, you will probably loose all
the extra functionality that OSF/1 has, and you'd be replacing the already
working gethostent() routines with the same things. Probably the reason you
didn't catch this is that the file is called host.conf in Resolv+ instead of 
svc.conf by DEC. And god knows I would hope that the shared clibs on the Alpha
don't need as much replacing as the very broken ones on SunOS did (though
I've already found a few possible bugs <sigh>).


