Typically, you request the administrator of the RIS server to register your 
client.  If you have access to the RIS server and root privileges, you simply
execute /usr/sbin/ris.  It is menu driven and will prompt you for all the
information you need to provide.

|>
|>Is there a way to go directly to v3?
|>	ie install v3 via remote CD
|>	would this be easier?
|>

The only way to go directly to V3.0 is by doing a full installation.  But that
is destructive and I assume you don't want that.  

It's not clear what you mean by "v1".  If you mean V1.2, then you use installupgrade to get to V1.3.  Once you are at V1.3 or later, you use installupdate to go to the next release.

Dave


