Of course Firewall services are available on the same platform
(see attached press releases).  However, the "Firewall Service"
(Historically known as S.E.A.L.) is one of some complexity
requiring considerable Internet expertise, TCP/IP network design
and namespace planning and design and very good general Unix 
knowledge.  It is not intended to package the "Firewall Service" 
in the same "out-of-the-box" fashion as the Internet application
clients.

You are quite right to point out that anyone considering a quick
connection to the Internet should not overlook the security aspects.
Digital sees this as a very important opportunity to deliver
quality Internet services to customers.  Your comments about proxy
servers and other features are also on the mark. We envisage large 
scale volume buying of the Internet ready Alphaservers (probably at
departmental level) - And in conjunction, special consultancy 
assisted services (such as Security, WWW Server Design, Network 
Facility Management, etc. ) - these being more directed to central 
IT, network or computer centre managers.

