Matthais,

When you configure DCE through the dcesetup script you are
asked a question about whether or not to configure SIA
security.  If you answered yes to this then you can proceed
(otherwise you'll need to reconfigure).

Anyway, once you've configured SIA security you need to
establish a UNIX user (i.e. /etc/passwd entry) and 
a DCE user (through rgy_edit) with the same account name
and password. Once you've done this you will only have
to do one login.

If this isn't quite right, forgive me. I don't have the
documentation handy right now, but the places to look for
more info on this are:

	Digital DCE Product Guide (On the OLD CDROM)
	System Administration: Security (On the OS CDROM)

There are some scripts to help you duplicate your existing
/etc/passwd entries in the DCE security database to assist
in setting this up. Check out the docs.

Cheers,

Tim.



