>I thought the alignment would be like this:
>[...]
>
>but I am getting this alignment
>[...]
>
>Could someone please tell me how I can get around this funny alignment
>arrangement ?

Count the bytes: the U32 field has two U8 fields and eight U16 fields
before it. Thats 2*1 + 8*2 = 18 bytes. Now since 18 is not a multiple
of 4 (the size of a U32), you get padding.

