In article <3bvrlg$ruq@mustang.smcvt.edu>,
Dave Goodwin <goodwin@smcvax.smcvt.edu> wrote:
> I'm showing my newbie status here, but we've not been on UNIX of any type
> for very long.  I need to add a line to the .profile of all our users and
> am wondering if there's a quick way to do so?  Thanks for the help...

Create two files:
	line-for-dot-profile
	line-for-dot-login

These contain the shell and csh versions of the line you want to add. Then
do this:

awk -F: '{print $6,$7}' /etc/passwd | while read directory shell
do
  case $shell in
    *csh) file=login;;
    *) file=profile;;
  esac
  cat line-for-dot-$file >> $directory/.$file
done
