In article <id.0JCF1.I34@nmti.com>, rwp@nmti.com (roland pringle) writes:
|>I am running on a DEC Alpha3000/OSF3.0.  I have read the man pages on
|>f77.  Can anyone tell me how to get a map of a fortran program.  There
|>is no switch setting in f77 for a map.  there is one on cc(-m).  Any 
|>help would be appreciated.

-m is actually an ld switch.  Unfortunately, f77 defines -m to have a
different meaning, so it "hides" the ld switch.  (A hazard of the UNIX
way of doing things.)  I would suggest using -o and -c to produce just
the objects and then use ld separately with the -m switch (and appropriate
libs) to get the load map.
