>We're having a problem with a DEC Alpha 3000 600 that has 64M of memory
>and 128M of swap space.  We're running OSF1.  I keep doing fine for a
>few days after rebooting and then we start getting 

>swap space below 10% free

I had this same problem.  What you are probably suffering from
is an overgrown xdm process.  Try adding the following line to
/usr/lib/X11/xdm/xdm-config:

DisplayManager._0.terminateServer:      true

take a look at the xdm man page entry:
  DisplayManager.DISPLAY.terminateServer
       This boolean resource specifies whether the X server should be ter-
       minated when a session terminates (instead of resetting it).  This
       resource can be used when the server tends to grow without bound over
       time, in order to limit the amount of time the server is run.  The
       default value is ``false.''

This forces xdm to release memory periodically...

This should definitely be in the FAQ (don't know if it is).

--tom


