The Net2 "su" command works fine under OSF/1.  Get the source from

ftp.uu.net:/systems/unix/bsd-sources/usr.bin/su

The only define it's missing is:

#define _PATH_DEFPATH   "/usr/bin:/bin"

(From paths.h in the Net2 distribution)

The Makefile is the new BSD style.  I suggest you avoid using it unless
you have pmake.  Instead:

cc -O -o su su.c

Works like a charm.

