Gerhard Nolte (gnolte@gwdu19.gwdg.de) wrote:

: One of the printers needs data in the format "Parity none, 8 bits, 1
: stopbit". What are the default settings of a LAT-port and how to change
: these settings ?

What type of terminal server are you using?

How the port settings are changed varies slightly from terminal server to
terminal server.  The basic format of the command syntax for many of Digital's
servers is "set port xxx".  Try "help set port" at the server console.

: If a terminal server is occupied by an other machine the LAT
: connection times out after some seconds. The lpd doesn't handle this
: error condition correctly. How to increase the timeout period for such
: a LAT-port?!

If the connection fails due to lpd not being able to access the port, lpd
should retry.

If you don't want your lpd connection requests to queue at the terminal server
when the port is busy (if your server supports this feature and it is turned on
for the particular port) and possibly confuse lpd, make sure that the printer 
application port tty is bound with queuing disabled, i.e. with the "-Q" switch 
on the command line.


