There are probably several packages.  We use one from Young Minds, Inc.  It's essentially a 486-based PC that connects to a DEC OSF/1 or ULTRIX system via the SCSI bus.  It acts as a buffer for the CD Writer.  We use a Kodak writer.

The package includes software for ULTRIX and DEC OSF/1 and allows you to create ISO 9660 and ISO 9660-Rock Ridge formats.  We create ufs disks by not using their software but a series of UNIX commands instead.

This setup is not cheap!!  The writer itself might have cost around $8k.

Dave


