JOHN HANSEN (john.hansen@dkb.dk) wrote:
: I'm using a AXP 3000, trying to get a modem working direct on the serial 
: port. 

What we did was to connect the modem to the serial port and run Kermit.
You can user Kermit in two different ways: (1) Use 'CONNECT' and talk
directly to the modem (e g, ATZ0 (initialize), ATDT5551111 (dial));
(2) Use the Kermit 'DIAL' command.

The serial port can handle 19,200 baud.  If you want the modem to auto-
answer, you'll need different software.
